  "70-745__f4728216237f7fa5": {
    "Question #: 1": {
      "Title": "Exam 70-745 topic 1 question 13 discussion - ExamTopics",
      "Question": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "HOTSPOT -"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You deploy Microsoft System Center Virtual Machine Manager (SCVMM) and System Center Configuration Manager in an Active Directory Domain Services (AD"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "DS) domain."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You must deploy a Software Defined Networking (SDN) network controller."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "You need to create the required AD DS security groups for management users and network controller clients."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Which members should you add to each group? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Hot Area:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/03408/0003900001.png"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {},
      "Answer": {
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Suggested Answer:"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/03408/0004000001.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "1. Create security groups for network controller management and clients."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 In Active Directory Users and Computers, create a security group for network controller management."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 In the group, add all the users who have permission to configure the network controller. For example, create a group named Network Controller Admins."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 All of the users that you add to this group must also be members of the Domain Users group in Active Directory."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 The group for network controller management should be a domain local group. Members of this group will be able to create, delete, and update the deployed network controller configuration."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Create at least one user account that is a member of this group and have access to its credentials. After the network controller is deployed, VMM can be configured to use the user account credentials to establish communication with the network controller."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "1. Create another security group for network controller clients"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Add users with permission to configure and manage networks using network controller. For example, create a group named Network Controller Users."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 All of the users that you add to the new group must also be members of the Domain Users group in Active Directory."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 All Network Controller configuration and management is performed using Representational State Transfer (DNS)."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "The group should be a Domain Local group. After the network controller is deployed, any members of this group will have permissions to communicate with the"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "image",
            "src": "https://www.examtopics.com/assets/media/exam-media/03408/0004000010.png"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "network controller via the REST based interface."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "\u2711 Create at least one user account that is a member of this group. After the network controller is deployed, VMM can be configured to use the user account credentials to establish communication with the network controller."
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "References:"
          },
          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/system-center/vmm/sdn-controller?view=sc-vmm-1801"
          }
        ]
      },
